WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.334 --> 00:00:19.097
The rain continued for a week, but Mary didn't mind.

2
00:00:19.098 --> 00:00:23.395
She spent hours every day with Colin in his room.

3
00:00:23.396 --> 00:00:27.452
They talked about rajahs and gardens and Dickon.

4
00:00:27.453 --> 00:00:31.985
They looked through Colin's books and took turns reading to each other.

5
00:00:31.986 --> 00:00:36.388
Colin was still pale and lying on his sofa.

6
00:00:36.389 --> 00:00:41.392
But Mary thought he looked much better when he was amused or interested in something.

7
00:00:41.393 --> 00:00:44.808
Mrs. Medlock noticed something too:

8
00:00:44.809 --> 00:00:51.322
Colin hadn't whined or had a tantrum since he and Mary had become friends.

9
00:00:51.323 --> 00:00:56.738
Mary still didn't want to tell Colin that she had actually seen the secret garden.

10
00:00:56.739 --> 00:01:02.991
But he seemed so pleased with the idea of the garden that perhaps she could trust him after all.

11
00:01:02.992 --> 00:01:09.281
She did want him to go outside and meet Dickon, unless of course he didn't want to meet Dickon.

12
00:01:09.282 --> 00:01:13.120
Colin was never happy when people looked at him.

13
00:01:13.121 --> 00:01:18.732
"I always hated that, even when I was little," he told Mary one day.

14
00:01:18.733 --> 00:01:23.681
"When I was taken to the seaside, ladies would stop and talk to my nurse.

15
00:01:23.682 --> 00:01:27.980
I knew they were talking about how I wouldn't live to grow up.

16
00:01:27.981 --> 00:01:31.541
Sometimes the ladies would pat my cheek.

17
00:01:31.542 --> 00:01:35.992
Once I screamed out loud and bit a lady right on the hand.

18
00:01:35.993 --> 00:01:39.550
She was so frightened, she ran away!"

19
00:01:39.551 --> 00:01:42.299
"She probably thought you were a mad dog."

20
00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:45.878
Mary did not approve of what Colin had done.

21
00:01:45.879 --> 00:01:48.427
"I don't care what she thought."

22
00:01:48.428 --> 00:01:54.541
Mary hesitated for a moment. "Would you care if my friend looked at you?"

23
00:01:54.542 --> 00:01:57.376
Colin lay back on his cushion.

24
00:01:57.377 --> 00:02:00.640
"I believe there's one person I wouldn't mind.

25
00:02:00.641 --> 00:02:04.872
It's that boy who knows where the foxes live—Dickon.

26
00:02:04.873 --> 00:02:10.205
The birds and other animals aren't bothered by him," Colin said, still thinking it over.

27
00:02:10.206 --> 00:02:13.246
"So perhaps I wouldn't mind either.

28
00:02:13.247 --> 00:02:17.967
He's a sort of animal charmer, and I'm a sort of boy animal."

29
00:02:17.968 --> 00:02:23.090
And at that he and Mary both burst into laughter.

30
00:02:23.091 --> 00:02:29.740
On the first morning when the sky was blue again, Mary woke up before anyone else.

31
00:02:29.741 --> 00:02:33.386
She ran to her window and opened it.

32
00:02:33.387 --> 00:02:39.356
The moor looked so blue, and the singing birds sounded like an orchestra warming up.

33
00:02:39.357 --> 00:02:43.596
A gust of fresh, scented air blew into the room.

34
00:02:43.597 --> 00:02:46.649
Mary stuck her hand out the window.

35
00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:52.184
"It's warm! That will make the flowers push up and up in the garden."

36
00:02:52.185 --> 00:02:57.066
She leaned out the window and drew in great breaths of fresh air.

37
00:02:57.067 --> 00:03:03.323
Suddenly she had an idea. "I can't wait! I'm going to see the garden!"

38
00:03:03.324 --> 00:03:06.460
By now Mary could dress herself.

39
00:03:06.461 --> 00:03:11.101
In five minutes she had put on her clothes and run outside.

40
00:03:11.102 --> 00:03:14.310
The beautiful day filled her with joy.

41
00:03:14.311 --> 00:03:19.100
When she reached the door to the secret garden, she stopped.

42
00:03:19.101 --> 00:03:21.580
Caw! Caw!

43
00:03:21.581 --> 00:03:28.170
Mary looked up. There, on top of the wall, was a big black crow.

44
00:03:28.171 --> 00:03:33.419
Mary had never seen a crow up close before, and she was a little nervous.

45
00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:40.228
Just as she was wishing it would go away, it flew into the secret garden.

46
00:03:40.229 --> 00:03:46.317
When Mary pushed open the door, she saw that the crow was perched in an apple tree.

47
00:03:46.318 --> 00:03:52.888
A fox was lying underneath the tree, and they were both watching Dickon digging in the ground.

48
00:03:52.889 --> 00:03:57.226
"Oh, Dickon! You're here!" cried Mary.

49
00:03:57.227 --> 00:04:00.857
"I couldn't stay away when the garden was waiting."

50
00:04:00.858 --> 00:04:04.757
The crow flew down and landed on Dickon's shoulder.

51
00:04:04.758 --> 00:04:11.145
"This is Soot," he said. The red fox wandered over to meet Mary.

52
00:04:11.146 --> 00:04:16.538
"And this is Captain. Now you must see what's new in the garden."

53
00:04:16.539 --> 00:04:21.653
The two children ran from one part of the garden to another.

54
00:04:21.654 --> 00:04:27.027
Dickon showed Mary the swelling leaf buds on the rose branches that had seemed dead.

55
00:04:27.028 --> 00:04:32.412
He showed her what seemed like thousands of new green points pushing through the dirt.

56
00:04:32.413 --> 00:04:36.180
And best of all, he showed her the robin.

57
00:04:36.181 --> 00:04:41.761
The bird was fluttering about, carrying bits of twigs and straw to build a nest.

58
00:04:41.762 --> 00:04:45.418
He had found a mate.

59
00:04:45.419 --> 00:04:50.032
While they worked in the dirt, Mary told Dickon about meeting Colin.

60
00:04:50.033 --> 00:04:53.324
"Do you really think he wants to die?"

61
00:04:53.325 --> 00:04:59.981
Dickon stopped digging for a moment. "No, but he wishes he'd never been born.

62
00:04:59.982 --> 00:05:04.157
Mother says that's the worst thing on earth for a child."

63
00:05:04.158 --> 00:05:08.075
"Colin is so afraid he'll grow into a hunchback.

64
00:05:08.076 --> 00:05:12.472
He says if he felt a lump coming, he'd scream himself to death."

65
00:05:12.473 --> 00:05:17.722
"If he were out here, he wouldn't be watching for lumps to grow on his back."

66
00:05:17.723 --> 00:05:20.563
"I know," said Mary.

67
00:05:20.564 --> 00:05:25.473
"I keep wondering if we could bring him here without anyone seeing us."

68
00:05:25.474 --> 00:05:30.240
Just then the robin landed nearby with a twig in its beak.

69
00:05:30.241 --> 00:05:34.097
"Keep building your nest," Dickon said to the bird.

70
00:05:34.098 --> 00:05:39.247
"You know we won't bother you. We're building a nest too.

71
00:05:39.248 --> 00:05:46.664
Just be sure you keep this garden a secret."
